Maintainer: Oliver Glas <oliver.glas@inss.ch>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13)
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: caldun
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, lm-sensors, jq, libnotify-bin
Recommends: python3-gi, gir1.2-gtk-3.0, gir1.2-matepanelapplet-4.0
Description: report trustworthy machine temperatures and alert when hot
 caldun auto-discovers a machine's reliable temperature sensors (CPU,
 GPU and drives) from lm-sensors and reports them, flagging anything running
 warm or critical. Super-I/O chips that misreport temperatures on many boards
 (e.g. nct6798 on AMD systems) are ignored by default.
 .
 Alert thresholds are hybrid: the hardware-reported limit is used where the
 sensor provides one, otherwise a configurable per-category default applies;
 when both exist the more conservative value wins. Everything is overridable
 in /etc/caldun.conf, and "caldun --check" shows what will be
 monitored on the current machine.
 .
 The package installs a per-user systemd timer that runs the check every two
 minutes and raises a desktop notification when a sensor crosses its threshold.
 .
 On Ubuntu and Linux Mint with the MATE desktop, a panel applet
 (caldun-applet) is also installed. Right-click the MATE panel,
 choose "Add to Panel", and select "Caldun" to enable it.
 The applet shows live CPU, GPU, and drive temperatures colour-coded by
 status and refreshes every two minutes.
